{"id":8190468,"docketId":65288235,"caseName":"Southern Nebraska Power Co. v. Nebraska ex rel. Sorensen","caseNameFull":"Southern Nebraska Power Co. v. Nebraska ex rel. Sorensen, Attorney General","slug":"southern-nebraska-power-co-v-nebraska-ex-rel-sorensen","docketNumber":"No. 603","dateFiled":"1937-01-18","dateArgued":null,"dateCertGranted":null,"year":1937,"scdbId":"","direction":"","votesMajority":null,"votesMinority":null,"disposition":"","posture":"","syllabus":null,"summary":null,"headnotes":null,"proceduralHistory":null,"attorneys":"Mr. B. F. Napheys, Jr., for appellants., Mr. Edwin Vail for appellee.","natureOfSuit":"","citationCount":1,"judges":"","jurisdictionType":"","opinions":[{"id":8152399,"type":"majority","typeCode":"020lead","perCuriam":false,"author":"","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":2038,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"majority\">\n<author id=\"AhH\">\n<em>Per Curiam:</em>\n</author>\n<p id=\"A9EM\">The appeal herein is dismissed (1) for the reason that the judgment sought here to be reviewed is based upon a non-federal ground adequate to support it, <em>Electric Co. </em>v. <em>Dow, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"94668\"><a href=\"/opinion/94668/electric-co-v-dow/#492\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Electric Co. v. Dow\">166 U. S. 489, 492, 493</a></span>; <em>Pierce </em>v. <em>Somerset Railway, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"94938\"><a href=\"/opinion/94938/pierce-v-somerset-railway/#648\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Pierce v. Somerset Railway\">171 U. S. 641, 648</a></span>; <em>Leonard </em>v. <em>Vicksburg Ry. Co., </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"96309\"><a href=\"/opinion/96309/leonard-v-vicksburg-shreveport-pacific-railroad/#422\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Leonard v. Vicksburg, Shreveport &amp; Pacific Railroad\">198 U. S. 416, 422, 423</a></span>; <em>Gause </em>v. <em>Detroit Trust Co., </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"8152124\"><a href=\"/opinion/8190193/gause-v-detroit-trust-co/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Gause v. Detroit Trust Co.\">297 U. S. 695</a></span>, (2) in so far as a federal question is sought to be presented, for the want of a substantial federal question, <em>Zucht </em>v. <em>King, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"100054\"><a href=\"/opinion/100054/zucht-v-king/#176\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Zucht v. King\">260 U. S. 174, 176</a></span>; <em>Sugarman </em>v. <em>United States, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"99316\"><a href=\"/opinion/99316/sugarman-v-united-states/#184\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Sugarman v. United States\">249 U. S. 182, 184</a></span>; <em>Texas &amp; Pacific Ry. Co. </em>v. <em>Texas, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"8151642\"><a href=\"/opinion/8189711/texas-pacific-ry-co-v-texas/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Texas &amp; Pacific Ry. Co. v. Texas\">296 U. S. 552</a></span>.</p>\n</opinion>"}],"citations":[]}